					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>SCP-327 was hit by a boat propeller 5-10 years before retrieval</p> </blockquote> <p>Oh the huge manatee!</p> <p>(had to be done&#8230;. =| )</p> <p>Also,</p> <blockquote> <p>after a series of inexplicable mental illnesses amongst citizens of [REDACTED], Florida</p> </blockquote> <p>How could they tell? Dohhh ho ho ho ho ho =|</p> <p>Okay I'll stop.</p> <p>Overall, cute, but has no hook. I'm a proponent of keeping in SCPs that don't do anything but be weird, but I feel like the existence of the log at the end was going to be a setup to something interesting, and then it went nowhere. It's not really necessary if the article is to stay the way it is now, and at worst, it's a red herring</p> 
				 	]]>
